<node id="title" type="text" x="0" y="0" width="560" height="140" text-style="h1" text-align="left" vertical-align="top">

Turn SQL into a canvas that runs itself.

</node>

<node id="intro" type="text" x="0" y="160" width="520" height="120" text-align="left" vertical-align="top">

Every node is a DuckDB query, running here in your browser. Pick a station: the nodes reading it run again. Drag them around, edit the SQL, draw on it.

</node>

<node id="open-app" type="link" x="0" y="300" width="200" height="60" href="https://app.dash.builders/">

Open the app

</node>

<node id="extension" type="link" x="220" y="300" width="220" height="60" href="https://github.com/gropaul/dash" variant="outline">

DuckDB extension

</node>

<node id="stations" type="query" x="660" y="0" width="520" height="300">

```sql stations
-- view: select
-- column: StationName
SELECT StationName, count(DISTINCT TrainNumber) AS num_trains
FROM 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gropaul/dash-ui/main/test/data/services-2025-38.parquet'
GROUP BY ALL
ORDER BY num_trains DESC
```

</node>

<node id="types" type="query" x="660" y="360" width="520" height="460">

```sql types_of_trains
-- view: table
SELECT ServiceType, count(DISTINCT TrainNumber) AS num_trains
FROM 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gropaul/dash-ui/main/test/data/services-2025-38.parquet'
WHERE StationName IN (SELECT StationName FROM refs.stations())
GROUP BY ALL
ORDER BY num_trains DESC
```

</node>

<node id="total" type="query" x="1260" y="0" width="320" height="200" code="hidden">

```sql total_trains
-- view: text
SELECT format('{:,}', sum(num_trains)) AS total_trains, 'trains through the picked stations' AS detail
FROM refs.types_of_trains()
```

</node>

<node id="chart" type="query" x="1260" y="300" width="520" height="520" code="hidden">

```sql types_bar_chart
-- view: bar
-- x: ServiceType
-- y: num_trains
SELECT * FROM refs.types_of_trains()
```

</node>
